  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, be a point. A straight line drawn through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;parallel to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis crosses the ellipse and its auxiliary circle at points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, in the first quadrant. The tangent to the ellipse at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;intersects the positive&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math>. Suppose the straight line joining&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;and the origin makes an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi></math>&nbsp;with the positive&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, then the area of the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>II</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, then the area of the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, then the area of the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>IV</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>, then the area of the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The correct option is:</p>",
